# CANONICAL fixture — kernel-hardening WP-G: the fillet acceptance envelope's
# two blend classes, on the wire (SCHEMA §7.3 "Two blend classes, two budgets",
# §7.2 warning `FILLET_BLEND_APPROXIMATED`).
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES. OCCT builds a fillet in one of two ways. On a KPart corner it
# has a closed form and the blend face is a torus/cylinder/cone — ANALYTIC, exact
# to 2e-16. On anything else it WALKS the blend and fits a B-spline within its own
# approximation tolerance — APPROXIMATED, and the section radius then wobbles by
# ~1e-3 mm. Before WP-G both were judged by the same 1e-9 gate, so every walked
# blend was REFUSED `FILLET_SEMANTIC_CHECK_FAILED` — which is every
# boss-on-a-shaft and every oblique rim a daily-driver part needs
# (finding fillet-chamfer-1). Now the class is measured and each gets the budget
# that fits what it IS, and an approximated blend that publishes says so.
#
# THE TWO BODIES, one plan, so the contrast is same-radius and same-run:
#   `body_op1` — a Ø40 shaft (a r=20 circle on XZ extruded 60 symmetric about the
#     XZ plane) with a Ø20 boss fused on (a r=10 circle on XY extruded 40 up).
#     Their intersection is a cylinder/cylinder tee whose seam OCCT splits into
#     the tangent pair `e:1` + `e:4`; a fillet there is APPROXIMATED.
#   `body_op5` — a 40 x 20 x 20 box parked at x >= 60 so it cannot interact. Its
#     vertical edge `e:1` is plane/plane, so a fillet there is ANALYTIC.
# Both are filleted at r = 2.0. One warns; the other is silent. That is the whole
# claim, and running them in one session is what makes it a controlled comparison
# rather than two anecdotes.
#
# ONE VOCABULARY. The evidence is exactly the `blendEvidence` object a REFUSAL
# already emits (`maximumSectionRadiusError`, `allowedSectionRadiusError`,
# `maximumTangencyRadians`, `allowedTangencyRadians`, the section radii,
# `coordinateMagnitude`, the two face counts) plus `blendSurfaceClass`,
# `approximationTolerance`, `maxContourVertexValence` and the two counts
# `approximatedContours` / `approximatedBlendFaces`. There are NO alias
# spellings; `test_fillet_acceptance_envelope.cpp` asserts their absence, because
# two names for one number is how the two tracks drift apart.
#
# WHAT IS PINNED, AND WHAT IS NOT. Everything a reader BRANCHES on is literal:
# the warning's `code`, `severity`, `stage`, `evidence.blendSurfaceClass`, and the
# counts (`approximatedContours`, `approximatedBlendFaces`, `generatedFaceCount`,
# `supportFaceCount`, `boundaryCount`, `sampleCount`, `maxContourVertexValence`).
# The MEASUREMENTS are `$any`: `maximumSectionRadiusError`,
# `maximumTangencyRadians`, the section radii and `coordinateMagnitude` are
# OCCT's arithmetic, not a protocol fact, and `json_subset` compares numbers
# exactly — NDJSON is the wrong instrument for a value allowed to move in its
# last bits. Their measured pins live in
# `worker/tests/test_fillet_acceptance_envelope.cpp`, which asserts case 1 at
# 1.97e-3 mm +/-10 % and 1.24e-5 rad +/-20 % (and case 2 at 2.87e-3 / 4.94e-6) —
# the numbers SCHEMA §14 records.
#
# `allowedSectionRadiusError` IS literal (0.02) because it is not a measurement:
# it is `min(r x kRelSection, kSectionCeiling)` = `min(2 x 0.01, 0.05)`, the
# budget the SCHEMA defines, and a change to it is a change to `kRelSection` or
# `kSectionCeiling` — which SCHEMA §7.3 makes a §14 entry with a new measurement,
# exactly the thing that must not happen silently.
#
# `approximationTolerance` and `allowedTangencyRadians` are `$any` DESPITE being
# the same kind of thing, because the second is derived from the first
# (`min(max(1e-9, kTangencyFactor x tol / r), 1e-2)`, here 4 x 1e-4 / 2 = 2e-4 on
# macOS) and the first is whatever tolerance OCCT chose to fit this blend to. A
# Linux build of the same OCCT version may choose differently, and this file must
# pass on both. `kTangencyFactor` is pinned by the envelope test's margin
# assertion instead.
#
# `maxContourVertexValence` is 0 here and that is correct, not missing: the tee
# seam is a CLOSED contour, so its edge chain has no end vertex to count.
#
# The warning is the ONLY diagnostic on the seam step, and the box step's
# `diagnostics` is pinned EMPTY — the harness matches arrays element by element
# from index 0, so `[]` asserts "nothing", which is the half of the contract that
# says an analytic blend stays silent.
{"expect": {"v": 1, "t": "hello", "seq": 0}}
{"send": {"v": 1, "t": "req", "id": 1, "verb": "OpenSession", "args": {"documentId": "doc_fillet_approximated_blend", "documentRevision": 0, "workerEpoch": 4, "mode": "determinism"}}}
{"expect": {"v": 1, "t": "resp", "id": 1, "ok": true, "result": {"sessionOpen": true}}}
